# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS CONFIGURATION - EXAMPLE FILE
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# IMPORTANT:
# 1. Copy this file to .env: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill all values with your real credentials
# 3. NEVER commit .env to the repository
# 4. NEVER share .env via chat, email, or social media
# 5. Change permissions: chmod 600 .env
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TELEGRAM - Bot configuration
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get token at: https://t.me/BotFather
# Command: /newbot
TELEGRAM_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_BOT_TOKEN

# Comma-separated allowed chat IDs (no spaces)
# Get your ID at: https://t.me/userinfobot
ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS=123456789,987654321

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MyJDOWNLOADER - Account credentials
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create account at: https://www.myjdownloader.org
# Email and password of your MyJDownloader account
# (JD_* names are required by the antlafarge/jdownloader Docker image itself)
JD_EMAIL=your_email@example.com
JD_PASSWORD=your_secure_password_here

# Device name (registered in MyJDownloader)
# If not set, the system hostname will be used automatically
JD_DEVICENAME=MyJDownloader

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DOWNLOADS - Storage configuration
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path where downloads will be stored
# In Docker: /downloads (mapped to ./downloads)
# Locally: ./downloads
DOWNLOADS_PATH=/downloads

# Polling interval in seconds (how often to check for new downloads)
POLL_INTERVAL=10

# Maximum file size allowed in MB
# (files larger than this will be rejected)
MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB=50

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MINI APP API - CORS configuration (only needed once the Mini App frontend exists)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API (the Mini App's own origin).
# Leave empty for same-origin only (no CORS middleware added).
CORS_ORIGINS=

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# INSTRUCTIONS FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. Create .env file:
#    cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Fill in with your real values
#
# 3. Make the file secure:
#    chmod 600 .env
#
# 4. Run with python-dotenv:
#    pip install python-dotenv
#    python -m bot.main  # python-dotenv will load .env automatically
#
# 5. Or with docker-compose:
#    docker-compose up
#    (docker-compose.yml reads .env automatically)
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
